%N A364000 Numbers of the form (|2^i - 3^j| - 1)/2, i >= 1, j >= 1.
%C A364000 The terms up to (A014121(3000) - 1)/2 = 164128483697000103357, a(1)..a(2891), are proved (see A363999). - _Ruud H.G. van Tol_, Nov 10 2026
%H A364000 Ruud H.G. van Tol, <a href="/A364000/b364000.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..2891</a>
%F A364000 a(n) = (A363999(n) - 1)/2.
%o A364000 (PARI) upto(N) = if(N > 164128483697000103357, error("upto: N beyond the proved range")); my(S=List()); for(i=1, 70, for(j=1, 45, my(v=(abs(2^i-3^j)-1)/2); if(v <= N, listput(~S, v)))); Set(S); \\ _Ruud H.G. van Tol_, Nov 10 2026
